# Managed by home/srvs/claude-state.nix; edits here are overwritten.
#
# Merge policy, per file shape. The sync runs unattended every 5 minutes, so a
# conflict does not merely annoy someone — it WEDGES the sync for every other
# file until a human notices. Each rule below buys immunity from that for one
# class of file.

# Prose and notes: keeping BOTH sides' lines beats dropping one, and duplicated
# text is trivial to clean up. This is the right default for a *.md file whose
# shape git can safely treat as a bag of lines.
*.md merge=union

# ...which a MEMORY FILE is not, and the argument the *.json rule below makes
# applies here verbatim: a memory is a YAML frontmatter block plus prose, so a
# union merge can produce a structurally INVALID file. It did. Top's first merge
# fused two revisions of one memory into a document with two `description:` keys
# and a second `---` mid-body — no conflict, no log line, reads fine if you skim
# the prose, and silently malformed for every future reader.
#
# The driver resolves a memory as what it is — a statement of current truth —
# by last-writer-wins on the `modified:` timestamp Claude Code maintains itself,
# and treats MEMORY.md as the line-oriented index it is (union, then collapse
# what union duplicated). Both outcomes need no cleanup by anyone, which is the
# point: this repo is synced by an unattended timer every 5 minutes.
#
# Later rules win in gitattributes, so this must stay BELOW the *.md line.
# Requires merge.claudemd.driver, which claude-state-premigrate.sh sets on every
# run — without it this rule is inert and union silently applies again.
# Verified end-to-end by tools/claude-merge-test.sh (42 assertions).
**/memory/*.md merge=claudemd

# Transcripts and history.jsonl are append-only streams of independent JSON
# objects, one per line. Union keeps every line from both machines; interleaved
# order is cosmetically odd and semantically fine. Without this, history.jsonl —
# which BOTH machines append to constantly — would conflict on essentially every
# merge and stop the whole sync.
*.jsonl merge=union

# Settings and manifests are structured JSON, where a union merge produces a
# syntactically INVALID file. `ours` keeps this machine's copy when both sides
# changed the same file; when only one side changed it git still takes that
# change normally, so the file does still sync. Requires merge.ours.driver=true
# in the repo config — claude-state-premigrate.sh sets it on every run.
*.json merge=ours
